{
 "_readme": "Facts to fix by hand after the collections sync, by Wikidata id: any field of public/data/collections.json (name, nameThe, museumWiki (the museum's Wikipedia title), native (its name in its own language: [{name, lang, code}], [] for none), museum, city, country, countryName, lon, lat, artists, culture, year, image). Set museum and country to null when a work is in many places (prints, scattered groups): it then gets no 'where is it?' card. 'culture' is who made it when there's no named artist, written so it reads after 'made by the …'. 'plural': true when the name is plural (the Moai were…). _cities renames towns Wikidata gives as a district. Buildings (kind: building lists) also take 'style' (P149, written to read after 'built in the … style'; null for none) and 'types' (what it is: the first is shown). Books (kind: book) also take 'language' (the one it was first written in) and 'topics' (nonfiction shelves, overriding data/../src/tags.ts). Music (kind: music): 'composer' {id, name, image, born, died, country, countryName} replaces Wikidata's when it names an arranger or a completer. People (kind: person): 'person' {born, died, birthplace, state, stateId, country, countryName, instruments (the main ones, in order)}.",
